<title>CHILE: SOCCER-CHILE BEAT COLOMBIA 4-1 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-CHILE BEAT COLOMBIA 4-1 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-07-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile beat Colombia 4-1 in a</p>
<p>South American World Cup qualifier Saturday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Chile - Marcelo Salas (16, 26, 41), Ivan Zamorano (90,</p>
<p>penalty)</p>
<p>Colombia - Hamilton Ricard (52)</p>
<p>Attedance: 75,000</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>		  P  W  D  L   F  A Pts</p>
<p> Paraguay    10  7  2  1  15  6 23</p>
<p> Argentina   11  5  4  2  16 10 19</p>
<p> Colombia    12  5  3  4  17 14 18</p>
<p> Chile	 11  4  4  3  22 14 16</p>
<p> Bolivia     10  3  5  2  15 10 14</p>
<p> Ecuador     11  4  2  5  15 13 14</p>
<p> Uruguay     11  4  2  5  11 15 14</p>
<p> Peru	  11  3  4  4  11 14 13</p>
<p> Venezuela   11  0  2  9   7 33  2</p>
<p>Playing July 6: Paraguay v Argentina, Peru v Bolivia,</p>
<p>Venezuela v Ecuador</p>
<p>Note: top four teams qualify for the 1998 World Cup in</p>
<p>France. Brazil qualify automatically as holders.</p>
</text>
